/target

# Working journal and tuning artefacts. Kept on disk, out of version control:
# they are scratch output of a measurement run, not part of the engine, and
# they go stale the moment the next run starts.
#
# They used to be ignored for a second reason -- that they named the reference
# engines used for measurement -- and that reason is void. Those names are now
# in NOTICES.md on purpose: naming what you read is what makes an independent
# implementation checkable, and hiding it achieved the opposite.
NOTAS_PROXIMA_SESSAO.md
dataset_*.epd
tuned_*.txt
tune_*.log
selfplay_*.log
resolvequiet.log
datagen_*.log

# Redes e leitores de OUTROS motores: uso interno de diagnostico, nunca
# comitados. O Coda e' GPL-3.0 e a rede dele e' artefacto dele; serve para
# responder "a fraqueza e' a nossa busca ou a nossa rede?", nao para andar
# neste repositorio.
*.nnue
src/nnue_externo*.rs
redes_externas/

# Compiled bridge library: a GPL-derived object archive, ~93MB, and
# optional -- build.rs links it only when present and falls back to the
# Rust path when it is not. Distributing object code would oblige us to
# ship its corresponding source; building it locally does not.
sfbridge/

# Ours, and not published. The engine is public; the machinery that trains
# it, tunes it and runs the bot is not, and neither are the trained weights
# themselves. These all live on the development machines.
treino_768/
treino_sf16/
patches_bullet/
tools/
docs/
*.bin
DESENHO_*.md
w_r2long.txt
